  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Zolgensma (onasemnogene abeparvovec-xioi), an AAV vector gene therapy. Version: 1; Original: 08/2/2023; Accepted: 09/15/2023; Effective: 11/1/2023.",
    "Encoded: closed SMA indication, approval criteria 1\u20137 and denial criteria 2\u20134. Denial 1 is failure to meet approval criteria. Genetic confirmation is a separate attestation.",
    "No concomitant SMA modifying therapy, e.g. nusinersen or risdiplam.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval 3 months; no reauthorization will be approved.",
    "Quantity (notes only): one infusion per lifetime; total dose not to exceed 1.1\u00d710^14 vector genomes (vg) per kg. HCPCS J3590.",
    "Limitations of use: safety and effectiveness of repeat administration have not been evaluated. Use in advanced SMA (e.g. complete paralysis of limbs, permanent ventilator dependence) has not been evaluated.",
    "Cautions (notes only): if liver function abnormalities persist \u2265 2 times ULN after the 30-day period of systemic corticosteroids, promptly consult a pediatric gastroenterologist or hepatologist. Acute liver failure has been reported; preexisting hepatic impairment may increase risk.",
    "Documentation and numeric laboratory results require manual review; baseline testing, timing and thresholds are encoded as a combined attestation. Duration, no reauthorization, lifetime quantity, dose and cautions remain notes only, so this pack remains partial.",
    "PDL status remains unknown. No evaluate-linked alternatives are specified."
  ],
